description:
Read bounded base64 file bytes with independent chunk SHA256 and next_offset. Pin expected_version from the first chunk. No 1 MiB total file limit. This tool is part of plugin `HeptaRuntime Mac Controller`.

MCP server instructions: Filesystem tools. File lines render as `N:hh|content`; `N:hh` is the line id edit tools target, and edit results are diffs with fresh ids, so edits chain without re-viewing files. Reuse returned content and ids; read complete relevant blocks, then act on them. Each response costs a round trip: first decide what you need next, then request every call that doesn't depend on another's result in that one response.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__heptaruntime_mac_controller_binary_read(args: {
  // Bind every chunk to the version returned by the first read.
  expected_version?: string;
  host: string;
  // Maximum returned bytes; capped at 64 KiB. Use next_offset until eof.
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
  path: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Page up to 16384 bytes of the immutable original native SDK payload by operation_id, independent byte offset and SHA256. Supports serialized CallToolResult success/tool-error or ErrorData RPC-error bytes, before operation metadata and transport normalization; at most 1 MiB per retained result. Payloads are encrypted at rest with trusted token-derived private keys and an authenticated ID/tool/policy/ledger binding. Token or policy changes require controller restart and then revoke old retrieval; there is no live file-reload revocation; stdio restart cannot recover ephemeral-key results. This API never dispatches, interprets or follows payload links. Missing/corrupt/overflow/unknown output never grants replay and does not prove an effect failed. This tool is part of plugin `HeptaRuntime Mac Controller`.

